cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "XR Collaboration Prototype 2: Multi-User Immersive Environment with Hand Tracking, Eye Tracking, and Collaborative Physics"
authors:
  - family-names: Merino
    given-names: Leonel
  - family-names: Cosmelli
    given-names: Diego
version: 0.0.1
date-released: 2026-06-16
repository-code: https://github.com/leonelmerino/xr-collaboration-proto2
abstract: >
  Research prototype developed in Unity 2022.3 LTS for studying collaboration
  in extended reality (XR) environments. Implements a multi-user LAN environment
  where participants interact with a Jenga physics simulation using OpenXR hand
  tracking and humanoid avatars. Includes automated eye tracking data logging
  (CSV) with gaze, pupil, head pose, and area-of-interest data.
keywords:
  - extended reality
  - XR
  - virtual reality
  - hand tracking
  - eye tracking
  - multi-user collaboration
  - Unity
  - HTC Vive
  - Jenga
  - biometric data
  - research prototype
  - OpenXR
license: MIT
funding:
  - name: "ANID Proyectos de Exploración 13250116"
    title: "Enhancing Collaboration in Extended Reality: Towards Self-Adaptive Systems for Multi-User Spatial Computing with Multisensory and Psychophysiological Feedback"
    funder: "Agencia Nacional de Investigación y Desarrollo (ANID), Chile"
